---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ClientMatrix from '../../components/ClientMatrix.astro';
import OfficialInstallNotice from '../../components/OfficialInstallNotice.astro';
import { CLIENTS_690, MCP_REGISTRY_ID, NODE_ENGINES, REA_PIN } from '../../data/clients69';
const toc = [
  { id: 'pin', label: 'Pin and engines' },
  { id: 'matrix', label: `${CLIENTS_690.length} client IDs` },
  { id: 'verify', label: 'Verify one client' },
  { id: 'copilot', label: 'Copilot CLI schemas' },
  { id: 'manual', label: 'Not a --client row' },
  { id: 'added-690', label: 'Added since 6.5.0' },
  { id: 'related', label: 'Related' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="REA 6.9.0 client matrix | rea.run"
  description="The 28 setup --client IDs in rea-agents@6.9.0, including CodeBuddy, Cline, LM Studio, and FreeBuff. Doctor checks, unverified rows, and the MCP Registry id."
  path="/docs/clients/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-toc hidden md:block">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-3">On this page</p>
        {toc.map((item) => <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>)}
      </aside>
      <article class="prose-page">
        <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/docs/install/">← Install</a></p>
        <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">Docs · 6.9.0</p>
        <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">Client matrix for rea-agents 6.9.0</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">
          Setup in <code>{REA_PIN}</code> can register REA’s local stdio MCP server with <strong>{CLIENTS_690.length} client IDs</strong>.
          The table matches the supported-agents table in <code>docs/getting-started/installation.md</code> at tag <code>rea-agents-6.9.0</code>.
          Skill-directory pitfalls stay on <a href="/docs/mcp-clients/">MCP clients and skill paths</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="pin">Pin and engines</h2>
        <p>
          Node for this package: <code>{NODE_ENGINES}</code>.
          That string is <code>engines.node</code> in <code>package.json</code> at tag <code>rea-agents-6.9.0</code>, and <code>npm view rea-agents@6.9.0 engines</code> on <strong>2026-11-13 17:02:45 CST (Asia/Shanghai)</strong>.
          The 6.8.0 breaking note is where the floor moved: Node 23 and 25 are unsupported, and the installer does not upgrade Node.
          Registry id: <code>{MCP_REGISTRY_ID}</code>. The registry entry launches the same npm package with <code>npx</code> and the <code>mcp</code> command. It is not a second distribution.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm">
          npm <code>latest</code> on that check was <strong>6.9.0</strong>. Runbooks on this site still pin the version, because the next minor can break contracts (<a href="/docs/breaking/">always-bump-minor</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm">
          The 6.5.0 release said SQLite snapshot inspection needs <strong>Node 24.x ≥24.15 or 26+</strong> with <code>DatabaseSync.limits</code>, and that Node 22 and earlier 24 cannot use that lane.
          The 6.6–6.9 highlight sections reviewed for this pin do not say that gate was removed. A Node 22.23.4 host can install 6.9.0 and still sit outside the 6.5 SQLite lane.
        </p>
        <OfficialInstallNotice lang="en" variant="brief" />
        <pre><code>{`npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 setup
npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 doctor --client codex --json
npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 doctor --skill --json`}</code></pre>
        <p>
          <code>rea setup</code> offers these agents in a multi-select. Existing REA registrations start selected. Newly detected clients stay available but unselected: detection is context, not permission to write a new registration.
          Explicit <code>--client</code> skips the question. Approve the dry-run before <code>--yes</code>. Restart the client afterward. Persistent registrations pin the package version that performed setup.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>npx skills add morluto/rea --skill reverse-engineer-anything</code> installs instructions only. It does not register MCP and it does not install Ghidra, JEB, IDA, or Hopper.
        </p>

        <h2 id="matrix">Supported <code>--client</code> values</h2>
        <p>
          Rows follow the 6.9.0 supported-agents table. Notes that name a path or a verification limit are from <code>docs/getting-started/client-configuration.md</code> at the same tag, or from the 6.8.0 / 6.9.0 release bodies.
          IDs that were not in this site’s 6.5.0 matrix: <code>codebuddy</code>, <code>cline</code>, <code>lm_studio</code>, <code>freebuff</code>.
          Trae loading and live DeepSeek API compatibility remain unverified in that client-configuration page. FreeBuff native loading is unverified in the 6.8.0 release. The Cline page documents acceptance tests for setup and does not state a live tool call.
          Confirm each ID on your machine with <code>setup --dry-run</code> and <code>doctor</code>.
        </p>
        <ClientMatrix lang="en" />

        <h2 id="verify">Verify one client</h2>
        <p>Substitute the ID from the table. Inspect before you write. The commands below use Cline’s CLI id. DeepSeek Harness is <code>dsh</code>, LM Studio is <code>lm_studio</code>, FreeBuff is <code>freebuff</code>.</p>
        <pre><code>npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 setup --client cline --dry-run --json
npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 setup --client cline --yes --json
npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 doctor --client cline --json</code></pre>
        <ol>
          <li>Pi reads <code>mcp.json</code> as strict JSON. Comments, trailing commas, a byte-order mark, or an empty file are invalid. Setup reports them instead of rewriting the file. Repair to plain JSON, then rerun. Follow <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR</code> when it is set. Reload an existing Pi session after out-of-band edits. A project <code>.pi/mcp.json</code> can hide the user entry.</li>
          <li>Qwen Code: <code>mcpServers.rea</code> in <code>~/.qwen/settings.json</code>, or <code>$QWEN_HOME/settings.json</code>. Personal skills are discovered under <code>~/.agents/skills</code>.</li>
          <li>Hermes: <code>mcp_servers.rea</code> in <code>config.yaml</code>, resolved from <code>HERMES_HOME</code> or the platform default (<code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes</code> on Windows, <code>~/.hermes</code> elsewhere), including <code>HERMES_DATA_DIR_SUFFIX</code>. Setup follows <code>active_profile</code>. An invalid sticky profile is reported; it is not silently written into the default home.</li>
          <li>OMP: one registration per profile. Run setup under each <code>OMP_PROFILE</code> or <code>PI_PROFILE</code> that should load REA. <code>disabledServers</code> hides <code>rea</code>; setup removes that name from the file it edits.</li>
          <li>OpenCode honors <code>OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR</code> (fixed since 6.4.0).</li>
          <li>DeepSeek Harness: follow the Cordis patch and launcher notes in upstream <code>docs/getting-started/client-configuration.md</code> at the 6.9.0 tag. That page says live DeepSeek API compatibility remains unverified.</li>
          <li>Cline: <code>rea setup --client cline</code> configures the CLI (<code>~/.cline/data/settings/cline_mcp_settings.json</code>, or <code>CLINE_MCP_SETTINGS_PATH</code>). The VS Code extension is <code>rea mcp add --agent cline</code>, not the setup id.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="copilot">Copilot CLI and schema size</h2>
        <p>
          For GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.95, <code>gpt-4.1</code> model metadata can block ordinary chat with REA’s full input-schema profile before a model request is sent (<code>compaction_static_context_blocked</code>, <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1554" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1554</a>).
          From <strong>6.8.0</strong>, input advertisements <strong>default to compact</strong>. Set <code>REA_MCP_INPUT_SCHEMA_PROFILE=full</code> when you need the previous complete advertised guidance (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/5975" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#5975</a>).
          The compact profile passed native chat and analysis with the full tool inventory on Linux in upstream’s loopback fixture for that older issue. If an entry still needs the variable spelled out, add this to the <code>env</code> object of <code>mcpServers.rea</code> in Copilot’s <code>mcp-config.json</code>, keep the other settings, and restart:
        </p>
        <pre><code>{`"REA_MCP_INPUT_SCHEMA_PROFILE": "compact"`}</code></pre>
        <p>Compact advertisements can drop nested schema constraints. REA still validates canonical inputs. The same environment variable is the switch for other size-capped hosts (Kimi / Moonshot). It is not a license to send a different tool than the one you named.</p>

        <h2 id="manual">Not one of the {CLIENTS_690.length} setup rows</h2>
        <p>
          The 6.9.0 install doc still describes Grok Bot as a manual hosted connector. Setup does not call the account connector API and does not treat <code>~/.grokbot</code> as aligned.
          Ask the Grok Bot chat to add a custom MCP server named <code>rea</code> that runs on the Bot’s computer: <code>npx -y rea-agents@6.9.0 mcp</code>.
          Do not put credentials in that command. <code>rea doctor --client grok_bot</code> reports the manual step. <code>rea uninstall</code> does not remove the account connector.
          Grok Build (<code>grok_build</code>) is different: it is a row in the table and uses local <code>config.toml</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          llama.cpp’s llama-server can launch REA through its native stdio MCP configuration. The 6.9.0 install doc calls this a manual connection, not an automatic setup client ID. It is not a row in the table above.
        </p>

        <h2 id="added-690">Added since the 6.5.0 matrix</h2>
        <p>
          The 6.5.0 table already included Factory Droid (<code>droid</code>), DeepSeek Harness (<code>dsh</code>), Qoder (<code>qoder</code>), Trae (<code>trae</code>), ZCode (<code>zcode</code>), Kimi Code (<code>kimi</code>), and WorkBuddy (<code>workbuddy</code>).
          Those rows stay. The 6.9.0 client-configuration page still says Trae loading and live DeepSeek API compatibility are unverified. It says WorkBuddy and CodeBuddy tool calls are verified.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>freebuff</code> — first in 6.8.0 (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/2736" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#2736</a>). Native FreeBuff loading and skill discovery remain unverified. Older releases reject the id.</li>
          <li><code>codebuddy</code> and <code>lm_studio</code> — named together in the 6.9.0 changes list. <code>lm_studio</code> requires a release after 6.8.0. macOS LM Studio <strong>0.4.26</strong> is the stated verification; Linux and Windows remain unverified.</li>
          <li><code>cline</code> — 6.9.0 setup registration (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/10128" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#10128</a>). CLI only for <code>--client cline</code>. Live tool-call verification is not stated.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="related">Related</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/install/">Install guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/mcp-clients/">Skill paths and the Claude Code directory pitfall</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/breaking/">Upgrade runbook, 6.0–6.9.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="/changelog/">Changelog through 6.9.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/rea-agents-6-9-0/">6.9.0 operator guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/setup-vs-providers/">Setup does not install engines</a></li>
        </ul>

        <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
          <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/rea-agents-6.9.0/docs/getting-started/installation.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">docs/getting-started/installation.md at rea-agents-6.9.0</a> — supported-agents table and MCP Registry section</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/rea-agents-6.9.0/docs/getting-started/client-configuration.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">client-configuration.md at rea-agents-6.9.0</a> — paths and verification limits</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.9.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">6.9.0 release</a> · <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.8.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">6.8.0 release</a> (FreeBuff, compact default, Node engines)</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/rea-agents" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">npm rea-agents</a> — latest 6.9.0 on 2026-11-13 17:02:45 CST</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
